VM worker lifecycle coverage
============================

lifecycle_test calls the production controlled-exit helper with real pdfork
PD_DAEMON children. Two workers share one label/window; after teardown both
children are reaped, their procdescs are closed, and both window references
are released. Empty cleanup is repeatable. An invalid procdesc simulates a
failed stop and verifies its window reference stays reserved in this parent.

The test does not apply provider worker protection or exercise vsock I/O.
Full SwitchBoard idle decline/explicit stop, startup failures, event-loop
faults with live protected workers, delivered socket lifetime, and parent
restart after failed termination remain integration gates. Registry references
are process-local and do not protect against reuse across parent restart.
Exit-event errors now retain the reference; failed procdesc-watch setup uses
the controlled-stop helper. The tests cover invalid-handle exit-event failure
and cleanup of a real child already reaped through its retained procdesc.
Actual failed-watch injection remains a full-provider test gate.

serve_test drives the actual vmd_serve loop with injected provider/listener and
event operations. lifecycle_failures covers startup stages, fatal event/accept
errors, successful quiescence and failed acknowledgement, checking queue closure
and provider destruction. worker_loop_cleanup accepts a client and creates a
real pdfork child standing in for a worker. It covers failed watch setup with
successful cleanup, failed watch setup plus injected EPERM on termination,
explicit stop, and idle refusal followed by explicit stop. Assertions check
window references at acknowledgements, reaped children and closed handles.
The denial fixture keeps a backup procdesc exclusively to recover its child;
production supervisor recovery is not simulated or certified. No protected
worker or real vsock transport runs in this service-loop fixture.
